\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Gaussian coordinates for the three real types}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Use the scalar-column coordinates #{z_1,\ldots,z_r\in D^m} from the
proof of \ref{fdip-0050}. The centered equivariant real Gaussian of
\ref{fdip-0051} has density proportional to
##{\exp\left(-\frac12\sum_{a=1}^r
\operatorname{Re}(z_a^{\dagger}Q_\Xi z_a)\right).}
Its real covariance is the Hermitian matrix #{Q_\Xi^{-1}} on each
column. For #{D=\mathbb C}, column multiplication by #{\ue^{\ui\theta}}
preserves the law, and the complex second moment is
#{\mathbb E[z_az_a^{\dagger}]=2Q_\Xi^{-1}}. For #{D=\mathbb H}, right
multiplication #{z_a\mapsto z_aq} by a unit quaternion preserves the
real quadratic form. Left multiplication by an arbitrary quaternion
need not. These are symmetries of the multiplicity coordinates, not
further graph symmetries.}
